  "description": "A Wednesday normalization of the project names the fixture fire-rating interpretation: Door 101's story ends on Wednesday, Door 102's property is fulfilled on Wednesday under it, and a Door 103 story that an application records on Thursday has no period. A Friday normalization of the project names literal comparison. From Friday Door 101's sides disagree again: maintenance records, in the normalization's own write, a related story whose detection relates to the first and whose beginning, on Friday, cites the Friday normalization. The Door 103 story stays ended with no period, and its sides' Friday disagreement is a related story in the same way. Door 102 stays fulfilled at its Wednesday qualifying moment. A Saturday frame resolves to literal comparison and names the Friday normalization; Tuesday and Thursday frames read as they did before the Friday normalization was recorded.",
  "note": "7.3.8: \"A later normalization of the same scope Item supersedes it from that later act's own effective time\"; *After it*: \"Sides that become unequal at T begin to disagree at T, and where their story had ended, the disagreement is a related story (7.3.2), whose beginning cites the normalization (7.6.4).\" 7.2.6: a story with no period \"stays ended, and a later disagreement of its sides, through later evidence or a later normalization, is a related story (7.3.2, 7.3.8).\" 6.5.2: \"Fulfillment, once it occurs, is not reversed by anything that happens after the qualifying moment\". README section 7, Normalizations: \"`generated` lists any related story or other story record that maintenance records because of it\"; the two generated detections are matched in any order.",
